# Auto commit and push

When a task produces meaningful code/config changes and work on that change set is done:

1. Commit with a concise message (follow repo style; stage only relevant files).
2. `git push` to the tracked remote branch immediately after a successful commit.
3. Do not wait for the user to say「提交」or「push」unless they explicitly asked to hold off, or the change is secrets/credentials only.

Still respect: no force-push to main/master, no amending pushed commits, no skipping hooks, no committing secrets.
